Subject: [PATCH 1/3] llama: pin the attention Q/K/V projections into the graph
 first (+0.5% decode)

cgraph order is the dependency DFS, not the creation order, so the stock
qwen35moe attention block emits

    wq | q_norm | rope_q | wk , wv | k_norm | rope_k

and every one of the three launch-grouping mechanisms the CUDA backend already
has is broken by the node that sits between its members:

  * wq cannot lead a grouped mmvq launch with wk/wv - hoisting the K projection
    over q_norm's write is range-blocked by ggml-alloc;
  * q_norm cannot lead a grouped rms_norm launch with k_norm, because k_norm's
    own input is written by the skipped-over wk matvec;
  * rope_q cannot lead a grouped rope launch with rope_k for the same reason one
    level down.

Expanding the three projections into the graph first makes the members adjacent,
so no hoist is needed at all and the groups form on the trivially-legal path.
Ops, operands, shapes and every arithmetic expression are unchanged - only the
position in the node list. Decode only (n_tokens == 1); at prefill none of the
grouped launches is on the route and the stock order is kept.

Measured: the QK-norm pair groups (-10 dispatches/token). The Q/K/V matvec group
still declines because attn_q is Q6_K while attn_k/attn_v are Q8_0 and the
grouped mmvq kernel is single-type; that one needs 0047's two-quant-types-in-one
-launch machinery and is left for a later patch.

GGML_QWEN_ATTN_QKV_PIN=0 restores the stock node order.
---
 src/models/qwen35moe.cpp | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

